  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd a shared public ownership procedure under `issue-claims`. Connect the coordinator, startup relays, worker and reviewer agents, and the four dispatch skills.\n\n- Keep one writer record with the live issue claim and one counted reviewer record on the PR.\n- Pass the record URL, unique worker identity, exact base and starting head to each actor.\n- Distinguish caller-dispatched workers from self-started workers. Do not create a second claim for a dispatched worker.\n- Count reviewer records only from base-repository collaborators. Contributor pre-checks claim no reviewer ownership, marker or labels.\n- Keep the existing contributor claim tests: an open PR, a branch commit within 48 hours, or an issue comment within 48 hours. Keep the owner-account 4-hour rule.\n- Require reviewers to read before work, re-read before a verdict or labels, and release on completion, skip or confirmed failure.\n- Stand down on live owners. Stop on moved remote heads or rejected pushes. Never force-push.\n- Compile affected code before a refresh push, including clean merges. Check each affected package with `-p`, also for shared inputs such as `Cargo.lock`.\n- Preserve the local review lock, refresh timing and existing merge-trial validation.\n\nThis is a cooperative procedure, not an atomic distributed lock. Concurrent comments and a race after the last read remain possible. Tests check the published instructions, not agent compliance or distributed exclusion. The decision file records the alternatives and limits.\n\n## Review fixes\n\nCommit `9869b54f5b26dbfe904952de93c46d62ed893b6b` addresses the three findings in the collaborator review of `0099e66d4f855841fcd7169545d1d167a9d446c3`:\n\n1. Connect `coordinator.md` and `start-orchestrator`. Reconcile delegated and self-started claims in `work-issue`.\n2. Restrict counted reviewer ownership to collaborators. State all existing writer activity tests and explicit release rules.\n3. Pass the record URL in the review dispatch prompt. Connect the full lifecycle in `PR-reviewer.md` and delta-review briefs.\n\nThe same commit clarifies per-package refresh checks and replaces unnecessary full-sentence assertions with shorter contract phrases. The new head needs a fresh independent review. The earlier review does not approve it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask --bin xtask ownership_contract_tests -- --nocapture`: 13 passed.\n- Three test-first runs demonstrated the missing dispatch, authority and reviewer contracts before their fixes.\n- The final 13 contracts replayed against the actual pre-fix documents at `0099e66d4` give four passes and nine expected failures. The final documents pass all 13.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 cargo xtask gate quick --base bd467a0ccf581f3f700209247b62e6949ab7735e`: passed on the final committed tree. One real xtask step ran in 232 seconds. Its 12 targets reported 408 passed, zero failed and zero ignored.\n- `cargo check --tests -p xtask`: passed.\n- Strict Clippy reproduces existing `clippy::needless_bool` at `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67`. That file matches both the original base and fetched main. `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings -A clippy::needless_bool`: passed. This is not a strict Clippy pass.\n- `rustfmt --edition 2021 --check xtask/src/ownership_contract_tests.rs`: passed. Package-wide `cargo fmt --check -p xtask` still reports existing formatting differences. No broad formatting changes were made.\n- Nine relative Markdown links, code fences, final newlines, exact file scope and added-line security scan: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed. Read-only `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main HEAD`: clean.\n\nNo application, GUI, catalog-generation, light, heavy or release lane ran for this process-only change. The quick step includes existing synthetic catalog-tool tests. No production CAM code, dependencies or workflows changed. No maintainer runner was used.\n\n## Ownership and scope\n\nCurrent writer record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3661#issuecomment-7195701842\n\nOriginal claim: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3661#issuecomment-7185068834\n\nThe original branch starts at `bd467a0ccf581f3f700209247b62e6949ab7735e`. The current writer record captures the PR-reported base at dispatch time, not the original branch point. No main refresh was made for this rework. The cumulative diff contains only the 12 intended process, decision and contract-test files.\n\nAuthenticated branch-rules and rulesets reads returned empty lists. Legacy protection and required-check endpoints returned 404, not successful empty configurations. No CI checks are reported. No green CI result is inferred.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #3661\n",
